Pada halaman peringkat global (`app/(student)/leaderboard/page.tsx:34-42`):
```tsx
for (const course of allCourses) {
  const ranked = await getCourseLeaderboard(course.id);
  // ...
}
```
- Jika mahasiswa atau admin terdaftar di 8 kelas, halaman akan menunggu 8 kueri database yang dieksekusi secara berurutan (*waterfall/serial*), memperlambat waktu muat awal (TTFB).
- Jika salah satu kelas mengalami kegagalan kueri, seluruh halaman leaderboard akan melempar unhandled exception dan gagal dimuat.
- **Rekomendasi:**
  - Gunakan `Promise.allSettled` atau `Promise.all` dengan pembungkus `try/catch` defensif per kelas agar kueri berjalan paralel dan toleran terhadap kegagalan parsial.

---

Each learning section contains:

- stable `id`, `chapterId`, `title`, `slug`, and zero based `orderIndex`;
- optional `parentSectionId`;
- one `learningObjective`;
- `primaryIdeaIds`, `supportingIdeaIds`, and `sourceChunkIds`.

The hierarchy is acyclic and limited to three levels. Sibling order and slug are unique. Display numbers such as `1.1` and `1.1.1` are derived from hierarchy and order, never stored as author supplied identity.

Every Idea belongs to exactly one primary learning section. Supporting membership is optional. Every referenced Idea and source chunk must exist in the bundle. Review exposes both the pedagogical order and all source mappings, so authoring may reorder material without losing traceability.

Each bundle contains `manifest.json`, `entities/products.json`, and `entities/dependencies.json`. The manifest declares `product-bundle.v2`, course identity, creator and curator, stable entity IDs, file checksums, bundle checksum, and unresolved conflicts.

Each product declares:

- stable ID, product type, version, `draft` status, and schema version;
- published Idea IDs, versions, semantic hashes, roles, and weights;
- active source material IDs, versions, checksums, and source excerpt IDs;
- creator, optional curator, source hash, generation hash, and optional AI metadata;
- product-specific renderable content.

Validation is pure and fail-closed. It rejects unsafe ZIP entries, unknown fields, checksum drift, duplicate IDs, missing solution questions, non-atomic flashcards, invalid assessment scope, holdout markers, and unresolved manifest conflicts. Dependencies with `NEEDS_REVIEW` or `STALE` make publication ineligible.

Every staged product must be complete enough to publish after admin inspection while remaining `draft`. External agents can use `$UPLOADER` and `$APPROVING_REVIEWER`; publication resolves those sentinels without exporting private user identity IDs. Legacy bundles containing `published` entities remain readable for compatibility, but new authoring must emit `draft`. A `withdrawn` entity cannot re-enter a draft bundle.

Additional product invariants are explicit in the bundle contract:

- every product Idea-link weight is finite, positive, and the product total is one;
- a flashcard references exactly one Idea;
- every question product declares one required `itbSource` with `referenceId` and a human-readable `eventName`, such as `UTS Matematika I ITB 2024`;
- the source reference is included in `itbCuration`, and publication accepts only `allowed` references whose stored `sourceLabel` exactly matches `itbSource.eventName`;
- a multi-Idea question declares a relation for every linked Idea, with an optional rationale, and uses the `analyze`, `evaluate`, or `create` cognitive level;
- every Diktat declares its source Article ID, version, and generation hash, and a matching product dependency exists.
- an Article passes the strict semantic compiler and required block coverage gate during upload;
- multiple-choice options use `{ id, text, isCorrect }`, carry stable unique IDs, and have a valid deterministic key;
- every question in the bundle has exactly one solution;
- correct-answer markers are excluded from Vectorize payloads and Zyra runtime hydration.

Each question uses this dedicated source block in addition to curation dimensions:

```json
{
  "productType": "question",
  "itbSource": {
    "referenceId": "itb-reference-id",
    "eventName": "UTS Matematika I ITB 2024"
  },
  "itbCuration": [
    {
      "referenceId": "itb-reference-id",
      "dimensions": {
        "difficulty": "similar",
        "format": "similar",
        "terminology": "similar",
        "reasoningPattern": "similar"
      },
      "curatorNote": "Reference verified against the source event."
    }
  ]
}
```

`itbSource` identifies the paper that must be cited. `itbCuration` records quality comparison and may contain additional allowed references, but those additional references are not treated as the question source. Missing source data, a holdout reference, a source not included in curation, or an event-name mismatch blocks publication.

The Authoring Context Pack exposes the required source metadata as `referenceId` and `sourceLabel` on each allowed benchmark summary. Its `id` remains the benchmark ID and is not valid as `itbSource.referenceId`. External authoring must match the exact event label against the source document, copy `referenceId` into `itbSource.referenceId`, and copy `sourceLabel` into `itbSource.eventName`.

Simpan di luar repo, misal `/tmp/run-next-staging.mjs`. Parser sederhana ini tidak pernah menampilkan nilai.

```js
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
for (const line of readFileSync("/workspaces/zyx-edu/.env.staging", "utf8").split("\n")) {
  const m = line.match(/^\s*(?:export\s+)?([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*=\s*(.*)\s*$/);
  if (!m) continue;
  let v = m[2].trim();
  if ((v.startsWith('"') && v.endsWith('"')) || (v.startsWith("'") && v.endsWith("'"))) v = v.slice(1, -1);
  if (!(m[1] in process.env)) process.env[m[1]] = v;
}
// build dan start butuh production agar lib/db memakai TURSO_* + token
process.env.NODE_ENV = process.argv.includes("dev") ? "development" : "production";
process.argv = [process.argv[0], "next", ...process.argv.slice(2)];
await import("/workspaces/zyx-edu/node_modules/next/dist/bin/next");
```

Pola sama dengan `scripts/staging/smoke-auth.ts`: ambil satu token sesi admin aktif, tandatangani lokal dengan HMAC, pakai sebagai cookie.

```js
import { createClient } from "@libsql/client";
import { createHash, createHmac } from "node:crypto";

// ENV sudah dimuat launcher; ulangi parse bila skrip berdiri sendiri
const client = createClient({
  url: ENV.TURSO_DATABASE_URL?.trim() || ENV.TURSO_CONNECTION_URL?.trim() || ENV.DATABASE_URL?.trim(),
  authToken: ENV.TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN?.trim() || undefined,
});

async function freshSignedCookie() {
  const r = await client.execute({
    sql: `SELECT s.token FROM pengguna p
          INNER JOIN pengguna_peran pp ON pp.pengguna_id = p.id
          INNER JOIN peran r ON r.id = pp.peran_id
          INNER JOIN session s ON s.user_id = p.id
          WHERE p.status = 'active' AND r.code = 'admin'
            AND (s.expires_at > ? OR s.expires_at > ?)
          ORDER BY s.updated_at DESC LIMIT 1`,
    args: [Date.now(), Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)],
  });
  const token = String(r.rows[0].token);
  const secret = rawSecret().length >= 32 ? rawSecret()
    : createHash("sha256").update(`zyx-edu:better-auth:secret-stretch:v1:${rawSecret()}`, "utf8").digest("base64url");
  const sig = createHmac("sha256", secret).update(token, "utf8").digest("base64");
  return encodeURIComponent(`${token}.${sig}`);
}
function rawSecret() { return ENV.BETTER_AUTH_SECRET; }
```

Tentukan nama cookie dengan probe, sekali per sesi server, dan probe ulang setelah restart server atau perubahan env:

```js
for (const name of ["better-auth.session_token", "__Secure-better-auth.session_token"]) {
  const res = await fetch("http://localhost:3100/api/auth/get-session", { headers: { cookie: `${name}=${value}` } });
  if ((await res.text()).includes('"user"')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ mode: name.includes("Secure") ? "secure" : "plain" }));
}
```

Saat memasang di Puppeteer, varian `__Secure-` butuh `secure: true`; localhost dipercaya Chrome sehingga tetap bisa dipasang di http.

Prinsip yang terbukti benar; menyimpang dari salah satu poin ini berpotensi mengulang eksperimen panjang:

1. Satu `page` baru per rute. Cookie segar dari `freshSignedCookie()` tepat sebelum navigasi, dipakai tepat satu kali.
2. Tema gelap lewat emulasi media, bukan priming `localStorage`. `ThemeProvider` memakai `attribute="class"` dengan `defaultTheme="system"`, jadi `prefers-color-scheme: dark` sudah cukup. Priming ke `/sign-in` sebelum navigasi target terbukti memicu kegagalan sesi.
3. `waitUntil: "domcontentloaded"` + jeda tetap (3 sampai 4 detik) + satu pass scroll untuk memicu konten lazy. Hindari `networkidle2`: halaman berat (analytics, jobs) tidak pernah idle dan selalu timeout.
4. Jangan pakai `page.setRequestInterception`. Pada pengujian kami, mengaktifkannya berkorelasi kuat dengan kegagalan sesi masif.
5. Validasi lingkungan di halaman pertama: bila muncul `ChunkLoadError`, hentikan crawl; itu tanda server lama menyajikan artefak build campuran, bukan masalah halaman.
6. Metrik per muatan: status HTTP, URL akhir (deteksi redirect ke `/sign-in`), `scrollWidth > clientWidth` (overflow), jumlah dan teks H1, error konsol, respons >= 400. Simpan screenshot `fullPage`.

Kerangka inti:

```js
const page = await browser.newPage();
if (variant === "desktop-dark") {
  await page.emulateMediaFeatures([{ name: "prefers-color-scheme", value: "dark" }]);
}
await page.setViewport(variant === "mobile-light"
  ? { width: 380, height: 844, deviceScaleFactor: 2, isMobile: true, hasTouch: true }
  : { width: 1440, height: 900, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });
await page.setCookie({ name: cookieName, value: await freshSignedCookie(), domain: "localhost", path: "/", httpOnly: true, sameSite: "Lax", secure: cookieName.includes("Secure") });
const resp = await page.goto("http://localhost:3100" + path, { waitUntil: "domcontentloaded", timeout: 60000 });
// bila finalUrl diawali /sign-in: ulangi sekali dengan token segar baru; bila tetap gagal, tandai gagal
await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 3500));
// scroll pass, evaluasi metrik, lalu:
await page.screenshot({ path: `artifacts/manual/${tanggal}/${slug(path)}/${variant}.png`, fullPage: true });
await page.close();
```

Varian standar agar hasil sebanding dengan audit sebelumnya: `desktop-light`, `desktop-dark`, `mobile-light` pada seluruh rute `app/(admin)/admin/**/page.tsx`. Rute dinamis memakai satu ID nyata per entitas lewat SELECT read-only (`courses`, `quiz_templates`, `blog_articles`, `google_meet_sessions`, `custom_forms`, `assessment_sources`, `impor_bundle` dengan filter `bundle_type`).
